From d9b93c2465e5a9c61a21efc52be45d0c48288703 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 11:03:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05898/11362] [outer-loop] find the native llama-cli hang fix
 two conductor tasks missed

Follow-up on last night's llama-cpp-python GPU fix. .484's exp5297 and
.485's exp5309 (two independent conductor tasks, a full milestone
apart) both hit a persistent hang trying to verify GPU offload through
a different, independent path -- the native llama.cpp-master CLI
binary, used as a cross-check against the Python bindings. Neither task
found the fix; both burned real wall-clock (549s and 206s) plus
repeated gate-block retries before giving up with
blocked_native_cli_timeout / generation_incomplete.

Reproduced directly: this build (b9606) defaults to an interactive chat
REPL. After answering a prompt it loops an empty "> " prompt forever
rather than exiting -- confirmed by running it myself and capturing
41+ million lines of blank prompts even with stdin closed via
/dev/null. exp5309's own command shows it already tried
--no-conversation (the obvious-looking fix) -- confirmed that alone is
insufficient. The flag that actually works is -st / --single-turn:
verified directly, clean exit code 0, "Exiting...", real
GPU-accelerated generation (~64 tok/s on gemma-4-31B-it, matching the
Python-binding fix's own numbers).

Documented in CLAUDE.md's Build Environment section next to the
llama-cpp-python fix (same investigation thread) and ops/known-issues.md,
so the conductor's next attempt at this gate doesn't rediscover it a
third time. Did not directly edit exp5297/exp5309's own experiment
scripts -- those are the conductor's own active research artifacts;
this is a documentation fix for whichever task picks up the gate next.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 CLAUDE.md           | 11 +++++++++++
 ops/known-issues.md | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 35 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CLAUDE.md b/CLAUDE.md
index 6c0a27eea7..e3df774485 100644
--- a/CLAUDE.md
+++ b/CLAUDE.md
@@ -3979,6 +3979,17 @@ Every user instruction must be captured and traceable to outcomes:
   the CPU-only wheel unless this build-flag requirement is applied again. Re-run the verification
   command above after any venv rebuild before trusting a `live_llm_inference`-substrate artifact's
   duration as GPU-backed evidence.
+- **The native `llama.cpp-master` CLI binary (`~/.cache/llama.cpp-master/build/bin/llama-cli`,
+  build b9606) hangs indefinitely on `-p <prompt> -n <N>` alone — needs `-st` / `--single-turn`,
+  not just `-no-cnv` / `--no-conversation` (found 2026-07-06, while `.484`'s `exp5297` and `.485`'s
+  `exp5309` were independently investigating this same hang across two milestones without finding
+  the fix).** This build defaults to an interactive chat REPL; `--no-conversation` alone does not
+  stop it from looping an empty `> ` prompt forever after answering (confirmed: hangs even with
+  stdin closed via `< /dev/null`, producing tens of millions of blank-prompt lines). `--single-turn`
+  (`-st`) is the flag that actually exits cleanly after one response — verified directly: real
+  GPU-accelerated generation (~64 tok/s on `gemma-4-31B-it` Q4_K_M, matching the llama-cpp-python
+  fix above), clean `Exiting...` and exit code 0. Any script driving this binary (or copying its
+  invocation pattern) should use `-st`, not `-no-cnv`, to guarantee termination.
 
